// currentConstrainedOut (constrained prefix for parser queries).
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// parser_validity (insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)):
//   - OpenConstrainedSpan sets currentConstrainedOut := [] and [] is a valid
//     prefix by parser.IsValidPrefix([]) (precondition). So invariant holds on
//     entry to the constrained phase.
//   - CloseSpanIfComplete: when closed==true it sets insideConstrainedOut:=false,
//     making the implication vacuous; when closed==false, state is unchanged and
//     invariant is preserved by induction.
//   - SafeRepetitionPenaltyStep returns either EOS or a parser-valid next token.
//     AppendConstrainedToken preserves parser validity (it only appends a
//     token that was produced by a constrained step). So the implication holds.
//   - On EOS from the inner step we break; insideConstrainedOut may still be
//     true but the loop exits and the postcondition is satisfied by the invariant.
// progress (|generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps):
//   - OpenConstrainedSpan appends "<<" and increments steps by 1, so the bound
//     is maintained.
//   - CloseSpanIfComplete: when it closes (costs 1 step), it appends ">>" to
//     generated (at most 1 token) and steps += 1; bound preserved.
//     When no-op (closed==false), generated unchanged and we do not charge steps
//     for the close query — the subsequent constrained step charges 1 step and
//     appends at most 1 token; bound preserved.
//   - SafeRepetitionPenaltyStep costs 1 step and AppendConstrainedToken appends
//     exactly 1 token; bound preserved.
//   - EOS costs 1 step, no token appended; bound preserved.
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END

generated := generatedPrefix;
insideConstrainedOut := insideConstrained;
currentConstrainedOut := currentConstrained;
cost := 0;

