// SMILES isocyanate CSD strategy.
// State tracked: generated (full visible output), insideConstrainedOut (whether
// we are inside a constrained span), currentConstrainedOut (the parser-tracked
// constrained segment), cost/steps (token budget).
//
// Design:
// 1. Append task guidance to steer the LM toward isocyanate SMILES (containing
//    N=C=O or [N+]=[C-]=O substructure).
// 2. Immediately open a constrained span (no free-text preamble needed since
//    the output contract is a bare SMILES string).
// 3. Inside the span, use SafeRepetitionPenaltyStep to discourage copying
//    exemplar tokens and GroupBoostedConstrainedStep with caller-supplied groups
//    to guide toward valid SMILES. When the parser branch factor narrows below a
//    threshold, fall back to plain AdaptiveConstrainedStep.
// 4. After each constrained step, speculatively check CloseSpanIfComplete; when
//    the parser reports completeness, close the span and stop.
// 5. EOS terminates the loop early.
//
// The hidden parser enforces SMILES grammar validity at every token position.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// parser_validity invariant:
//   - Before the loop: if insideConstrainedOut was already true, the precondition
//     gives parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut). If we call OpenConstrainedSpan
//     to force-enter, it sets currentConstrainedOut := [] which is valid by
//     parser.IsValidPrefix([]) (precondition).
//   - In the loop body (constrained branch, no-close path):
//     SafeRepetitionPenaltyStep and GroupBoostedConstrainedStep and
//     AdaptiveConstrainedStep all guarantee that the returned token is either
//     EOS or parser-valid next. AppendConstrainedToken extends currentConstrainedOut
//     by that token, preserving parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut).
//   - In the loop body (closed path): CloseSpanIfComplete sets
//     insideConstrainedOut := false, making the implication vacuous, and resets
//     currentConstrainedOut := [].
//   - EOS break: no state change; invariant trivially preserved.
//
