Strategy: // CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// SMILES isocyanate CSD strategy - HIDDEN CONSTRAINED CHUNK approach.
//
// The core problem with the previous attempt:
// - We opened a visible "<<" span IMMEDIATELY (entered_constrained_mode_too_early)
// - The span only contained 1 token ("O") - tiny span
// - The SMILES was never actually generated properly
//
// Root cause: The task says "Use the hidden parser-guided constrained chunk"
// meaning we should NOT use visible << >> delimiters. Instead, use
// ConstrainedGeneration directly to generate the SMILES, which uses the
// hidden constrained mode (no visible delimiters appended to generated output).
//
// Fix: Use ConstrainedGeneration(lm, parser, prompt, maxSteps, eosToken)
// which directly generates a parser-valid SMILES sequence without visible
// delimiters. The result is the SMILES string itself.
//
// This approach:
// 1. Appends task guidance to orient the model toward isocyanates
// 2. Calls ConstrainedGeneration which loops ConstrainedStep internally
//    until parser completion, EOS, or budget exhaustion
// 3. Sets cost appropriately
//
// The "hidden constrained chunk" means the parser controls generation but
// the output does NOT get wrapped in << >> visible delimiters.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// parser_validity: We do not enter insideConstrainedOut=true at any point
//   (we never call OpenConstrainedSpan). ConstrainedGeneration is a standalone
//   helper that manages its own internal constrained state without modifying
//   our insideConstrainedOut. So insideConstrainedOut remains false throughout,
//   and the implication (!insideConstrainedOut ==> currentConstrainedOut == [])
//   is maintained trivially. currentConstrainedOut stays [].
//
// progress: ConstrainedGeneration costs at most +maxSteps token-steps by its
//   contract, and appends at most maxSteps tokens to constrainedGenerated.
//   We set generated := generatedPrefix + constrainedGenerated, so
//   |generated| = |generatedPrefix| + |constrainedGenerated|
//             <= |generatedPrefix| + maxSteps.
//   cost := maxSteps satisfies cost <= maxSteps.
//   The final postcondition requires progress when maxSteps > 0:
//   if constrainedGenerated is nonempty then generated != generatedPrefix so
//   the progress disjunct holds. If it is empty we still have cost = maxSteps > 0.
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END

generated := generatedPrefix;
insideConstrainedOut := insideConstrained;
currentConstrainedOut := currentConstrained;
cost := 0;

if maxSteps == 0 {
  return;
}

helpers.AppendTaskGuidance(lm, "Generate a valid novel isocyanate SMILES containing the N=C=O functional group. Output only the SMILES string. Example structural patterns: alkyl-N=C=O, aryl-N=C=O, diisocyanate. Do not copy exemplars.");

// Use ConstrainedGeneration for hidden constrained chunk generation.
// This does NOT add visible << >> delimiters - it directly generates
// parser-valid tokens for the SMILES grammar.
var constrainedGenerated, terminatedByEos := helpers.ConstrainedGeneration(
  lm, parser, prompt, maxSteps, eosToken
);

// Append the constrained-generated SMILES tokens to our output.
generated := generatedPrefix + constrainedGenerated;

// We never entered a visible constrained span, so state is unchanged.
insideConstrainedOut := insideConstrained;
currentConstrainedOut := currentConstrained;

// Cost is bounded by maxSteps (ConstrainedGeneration costs at most maxSteps).
cost := maxSteps;

