// Root cause analysis:
// - CloseSpanIfComplete fires immediately when parser.IsCompletePrefix holds,
//   which happens after just one valid SMILES token (e.g. "C").
// - We need to keep generating until we have a SMILES that contains the N=C=O
//   group (isocyanate functionality).
// - The strategy must enforce a minimum constrained token count before allowing
//   closure. For isocyanate SMILES, we need at least ~7 tokens (e.g. "C","C","N",
//   "=","C","=","O" for CCN=C=O).
//
// Fix:
// 1. Use a minimum length gate: only call CloseSpanIfComplete when
//    |currentConstrainedOut| >= minLen (e.g. 7 tokens for CCN=C=O).
// 2. Keep using AdaptiveConstrainedStep for generation (no group boost needed
//    since the model just needs sufficient depth).
// 3. After generating enough tokens, allow CloseSpanIfComplete to close.
// 4. On EOS or budget, rollback to complete and close.
//
// The key insight: never close early. Isocyanates need N=C=O which requires
// at least 7 tokens in the constrained span. Gate closure on this minimum.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// parser_validity invariant:
//   - OpenConstrainedSpan sets currentConstrainedOut := [], which satisfies
//     parser.IsValidPrefix([]) by method precondition.
//   - In the loop, AdaptiveConstrainedStep returns EOS or a parser-valid next
//     token. AppendConstrainedToken extends currentConstrainedOut by that token,
//     preserving parser.IsValidPrefix by the contract of AppendConstrainedToken.
//   - CloseSpanIfComplete (closed=true): sets insideConstrainedOut := false,
//     making the implication vacuous, and sets currentConstrainedOut := [].
//   - CloseSpanIfComplete (closed=false, i.e., no-op): state unchanged.
//   - CloseConstrainedSpan: sets insideConstrainedOut := false, implication vacuous.
//   - RollbackConstrainedToComplete: ensures currentConstrainedOut is IsCompletePrefix
//     or [], both of which satisfy IsValidPrefix.
//
// progress invariant (|generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps):
//   - OpenConstrainedSpan appends exactly "<<" (+1 token) and steps becomes 1.
//   - Each loop iteration: steps increments by 1 per helper call (AdaptiveConstrainedStep
//     costs 1; AppendConstrainedToken costs 0; CloseSpanIfComplete costs 1 whether
//     it closes or not; CloseConstrainedSpan costs 1).
//   - The EOS branch: RollbackConstrainedToComplete costs 0, CloseConstrainedSpan
//     costs 1 and appends ">>" (+1 token), steps also increments by 1. Bound holds.
//   - Overall: each iteration increments steps by at most 2 (generate step + possible
//     close step) and appends at most 2 tokens, preserving the bound.
//   - maxSteps==0 || cost>0: when maxSteps>0, OpenConstrainedSpan fires first and
//     sets steps=1, so cost=1>0.
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END

